Apple's online store is going down for a few hours on a rolling country-by-country basis right now, but do not get your hopes up for new products.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2021/04/apple-store-down-feature.jpg" alt="" width="2067" height="1164" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-794754" /><br/>
Apple takes its online store down for a few hours ahead of Black Friday every year to tease its annual gift card offer with the purchase of select products.<br/>
<br/>
The store is down in <a href="https://www.apple.com/au/store">Australia</a>, <a href="https://www.apple.com/nz/store">New Zealand</a>, and <a href="https://www.apple.com/th/store">Thailand</a>, right now, and it will eventually go down in Europe, the United States, and Canada.<br/>
<br/>
In the U.S., Apple is <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/11/19/apple-announces-2026-black-friday-event/">offering gift cards worth up to &#36;300</a> with the purchase of an eligible iPhone, iPad, Mac, Apple Watch, HomePod, AirPods, Beats headphones, Beats Pill speaker, Apple Pencil Pro, and select other accessories. The offers will be available from November 27 through November 30 in participating countries.<br/>
<br/>
Many readers email us about Apple's online store going down ahead of Black Friday, so <strong>this is our annual reminder that it does not relate to new products</strong>. <br/>
